              "rationale": "The email input (name=\"jobs\") has no accessible name. The paragraph right before it, id=\"jobs-label\", says \"Want to work with us? Tell us your email.\" It is the input's visible prompt, and its id already suggests it was meant to be the label. Setting aria-labelledby=\"jobs-label\" gives the input that text as its accessible name, so the spoken name matches what sighted users see. This needs no new text. A reviewer may still want to change the <p> to a real <label for> element later, because that also makes the text clickable to focus the input. This patch fixes the finding but doesn't guarantee the page is fully accessible.",
